UID:0f867f0c-5422-4d44-93b8-d7faaae7019b@spacex-launch-alerts
DTSTAMP:20261114T021154Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261114T021154Z
SEQUENCE:216785514
SUMMARY:🚀 Starship · Starlink Group 31-2 (Starship Flight 15)
DTSTART:20261113T224736Z
DTEND:20261114T000236Z
LOCATION:Orbital Launch Pad 2\, SpaceX Starbase\, TX\, USA
DESCRIPTION:Status: Payload Deployed\nWindow: Fri\, 13 Nov 2026 22:45:00 UT
 C – Sat\, 14 Nov 2026 00:00:00 UTC\nOrbit: Low Earth Orbit\nPad: Orbital
  Launch Pad 2\, SpaceX Starbase\, TX\, USA\n\n▶ Watch live: https://www.
 youtube.com/watch?v=dl4O6RqbvOs\n\n15th test flight of the two-stage Stars
 hip launch vehicle and 4th flight of Starship V3. Second Starship flight t
 o deploy satellites (a group of Starlink satellites known as Starlink Grou
 p 31-2) into stable Low Earth Orbit and first ever to attempt returning th
 e Starship 2nd stage back to the launch site.\n\nThe ship is expected to f
 ly at an altitude approximately 275 km above Earth and complete approximat
 ely 14 orbits around the planet for more than 22 hours\, with the ship exp
 ected to attempt returning back to Starbase\, Texas on its launch pad by p
 ad arms catching.\n\nThe booster’s primary test objective on Flight 15 w
 ill be executing a successful launch\, ascent\, stage separation\, boostba
 ck burn\, and landing by pad arms catching. This will also be the 1st Star
 ship V3 booster to attempt returning to its launch site.\n\nStarship will 
 deliver 26 Starlink V3 satellites to orbit for the second time\, which aim
  to greatly expand the network's capacity and user speeds. Each Starlink V
 3 satellite will add 1 Tbps of capacity to the constellation. 3 of the sat
 ellites have been modified with a suite of cameras to scan Starship’s he
 atshield and transmit imagery down to operators.\n\nCountdown & updates: h
 ttps://benjaminowens612.github.io/spacex-launch-alerts/#0f867f0c-5422-4d44
 -93b8-d7faaae7019b
URL:https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dl4O6RqbvOs
CATEGORIES:starlink,starship
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
